--[[ ==========================================================================
     GAME DUMP  --  for Delta / mobile executors

     Saves everything readable about the game to local files on your device.

     OUTPUT  (in your executor's workspace folder)
       GameDump/tree.txt       full instance hierarchy with properties
       GameDump/remotes.txt    every RemoteEvent / RemoteFunction and its path
       GameDump/modules.txt    live data returned by every ModuleScript
       GameDump/scripts.txt    any script source that is actually readable
       GameDump/summary.txt    counts and an index

     WHY THERE IS NO SOURCE CODE
       Roblox strips Source from scripts before they reach a client. It is not
       a permission you can raise -- the text is simply not sent to your device.
       Delta has no decompiler, so nothing can recover it client side.

       What DOES work is require(). Requiring a ModuleScript gives you the real
       table it returns: configs, item lists, stats, prices, tuning values. For
       your own game that is usually the part you actually wanted.

       If you need true source for your own game, open the place in Studio --
       Source is fully readable there.
     ========================================================================== ]]

